---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const canonicalUrl = 'https://handheldsettings.com/rog-ally-settings/palworld/';
const title = 'Palworld ROG Ally settings: 720p/30 FPS baseline — Handheld Settings Lab';
const description = 'Start Palworld on ROG Ally or Ally X with a cautious 720p/30 FPS Low baseline, repeatable base and multiplayer tests, 900p comparison, and 40GB storage planning.';
const image = '/assets/games/palworld-header.jpg';

const sources = [
  { label: 'Steam: Palworld requirements, features, controller support, and official media', url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/app/1623730/Palworld/' },
  { label: 'Steam app-details API: current public product data for app 1623730', url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/api/appdetails?appids=1623730&cc=us&l=en' },
  { label: 'Pocketpair: official Palworld site', url: 'https://www.pocketpair.jp/palworld/' },
  { label: 'ASUS ROG: How to boost gaming performance on the ROG Ally', url: 'https://rog.asus.com/articles/guides/how-to-boost-gaming-performance-on-the-rog-ally/' },
  { label: 'ASUS ROG: ROG Ally (2023) technical specifications', url: 'https://rog.asus.com/gaming-handhelds/rog-ally/rog-ally-2023/spec/' },
  { label: 'ASUS ROG: ROG Ally X (2024) technical specifications', url: 'https://rog.asus.com/gaming-handhelds/rog-ally/rog-ally-x-2024/spec/' }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What Palworld settings should I use on ROG Ally?',
    answer: 'Start at 1280×720, a 30 FPS cap, the Low preset, and Armoury Crate Performance mode. Test a populated base, fast traversal, a multi-Pal fight, and the multiplayer state you actually use before raising image quality. This is a cautious editorial baseline, not a personally measured result.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Palworld run at 40 FPS on ROG Ally?',
    answer: 'Treat 40 FPS as a test rather than a guarantee. First pass the complete 720p/30 route, then change only the cap and repeat the same base, traversal, combat, and network conditions. Active Pals, world complexity, patches, Ally model, power mode, memory allocation, drivers, and thermals can change the result.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I use 720p, 900p, or 1080p for Palworld on ROG Ally?',
    answer: 'Validate 720p first because it provides a conservative diagnostic floor. Compare 900p only after the full route passes. Native 1080p is a clarity experiment, not the recommended starting point for a demanding open-world game with simulation and streaming load.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I use Performance or Turbo mode for Palworld?',
    answer: 'Begin in Performance mode for a repeatable battery-aware baseline. ASUS describes Performance as a balance between performance and battery life and Turbo as its maximum-power mode. Compare Turbo separately while plugged in only after the same test route is repeatable.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much storage does Palworld need on ROG Ally?',
    answer: 'Steam currently lists 40GB of available space and says an SSD is required. Leave additional free space for updates, shader data, world saves, captures, Workshop content, and Windows temporary files, and verify the live install estimate before downloading.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Were these Palworld ROG Ally settings personally benchmarked?',
    answer: 'No. Handheld Settings Lab checked current Steam, Pocketpair, and ASUS public sources but did not personally benchmark the current game build, world, server, Ally model, Windows build, driver, BIOS, Armoury Crate version, battery, memory allocation, or thermals. The 30 and 40 FPS figures are test targets, not measured locks.'
  }
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'TechArticle',
    headline: 'Palworld ROG Ally settings: 720p/30 FPS baseline',
    description,
    image: `https://handheldsettings.com${image}`,
    url: canonicalUrl,
    datePublished: '2026-08-23',
    dateModified: '2026-08-23',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab', url: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
    about: ['Palworld', 'ASUS ROG Ally', 'ROG Ally X', 'game settings', 'frame rate', 'handheld PC']
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'ROG Ally settings', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/rog-ally-settings/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Palworld settings', item: canonicalUrl }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: faq.question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer }
    }))
  }
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} image={image} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="wrap article">
    <span class="eyebrow">ROG Ally settings · Baseline published August 2026</span>
    <h1>Palworld ROG Ally settings: start at 720p and 30 FPS</h1>
    <p class="lede muted">Palworld combines open-world streaming, base automation, many active Pals, combat effects, and online state. This ROG Ally and Ally X workflow starts at a cautious 720p/30 FPS Low profile in Performance mode, then compares 900p or 40 FPS only after the same base-to-combat route passes. It is official-source-informed guidance—not a personally tested benchmark.</p>

    <figure class="game-hero">
      <img src={image} alt="Official Palworld Steam store header art showing Pals in an open landscape" width="460" height="215" />
      <figcaption class="media-credit">Official Palworld Steam store header image, saved locally from <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1623730/Palworld/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Pocketpair’s Steam store page</a>. Artwork and trademarks belong to their owners; editorial use does not imply endorsement.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="settings-panel">
      <section class="card"><h3>Safe first target</h3><div class="stat">720p / 30</div><p class="muted">Baseline to validate, not a lock</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Starting preset</h3><div class="stat">Low</div><p class="muted">Raise one control after full-route testing</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Second test</h3><div class="stat">900p</div><p class="muted">Compare clarity after stability</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Storage floor</h3><div class="stat">40GB</div><p class="muted">Current Steam requirement; SSD required</p></section>
    </div>

    <div class="callout"><strong>Test the world, not the menu:</strong> Steam explicitly notes that performance may vary with the number of active Pals. Use the same populated base, fast traversal path, raid or multi-Pal fight, weather, and intended multiplayer state for every comparison.</div>

    <h2>Recommended Palworld ROG Ally baseline</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Start here</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Armoury Crate operating mode</td><td>Performance</td><td>Creates a repeatable battery-aware first condition. Record the exact mode, charger state, fan setting, and manual power value if one is used.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Display mode / resolution</td><td>Fullscreen / 1280×720</td><td>Matches the panel’s 16:9 shape and provides a conservative diagnostic floor below 900p or native 1080p.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Frame-rate cap</td><td>30 FPS first</td><td>Prioritizes consistency through streaming, simulation, base activity, and multi-Pal combat. A higher target comes later.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Graphics preset</td><td>Low</td><td>Provides a cautious starting floor against demanding published desktop requirements without pretending it guarantees a handheld result.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Anti-aliasing / upscaling</td><td>Quality-class in-game option, if available</td><td>Start with the clearest normal reconstruction option. Avoid stacking it with RSR or another driver-level scaling path during diagnosis.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>View distance</td><td>Low</td><td>Reduces distant world rendering while a stable base and traversal profile is established.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Shadow quality</td><td>Low</td><td>Protects headroom during changing daylight, foliage, structures, combat, and busy bases.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Effects quality</td><td>Low</td><td>Reduces spikes during multi-Pal abilities, explosions, raids, and weather before nearby texture clarity is raised.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Texture quality</td><td>Low first; test Medium separately</td><td>Both Ally models use shared memory. Raise textures only after watching traversal, paging, and busy-area behavior.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Grass / foliage detail</td><td>Low</td><td>Large outdoor scenes can expose a different limit from interiors, menus, or a quiet base.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Motion blur</td><td>Off for comparison</td><td>Makes camera motion, scaling artifacts, and pacing easier to inspect. Restore later only by preference.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Control mode</td><td>Gamepad or Auto</td><td>Steam lists full controller support; a consistent Armoury Crate and Steam Input state reduces input-layer conflicts.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">Menu labels and available controls can change with updates. Photograph the current settings screen and use the nearest normal in-game equivalent. Do not install unofficial overrides merely to reproduce an older menu.</p>

    <h2>Run a repeatable base-to-combat test</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Finish updates and restart.</strong> Complete the stable game, Windows, MyASUS, Armoury Crate SE, graphics-driver, and BIOS updates offered for the exact Ally model.</li>
      <li><strong>Record the full state.</strong> Note Ally or Ally X, game version, world/save, server or solo mode, driver, BIOS, Armoury Crate version, operating mode, charger, memory allocation, resolution, cap, and graphics values.</li>
      <li><strong>Walk through a populated base.</strong> Include crafting stations, structures, storage, and the normal number of working Pals rather than testing an empty starter plot.</li>
      <li><strong>Traverse the same outdoor route.</strong> Use fast ground movement or flight through foliage, structures, enemies, and loading boundaries.</li>
      <li><strong>Repeat a demanding fight.</strong> Include several active Pals and visible abilities when practical. A quiet one-enemy encounter is not representative.</li>
      <li><strong>Match the intended network state.</strong> If the real use is multiplayer, compare on the same server and similar population; server or network delay is not automatically a graphics problem.</li>
      <li><strong>Change one variable.</strong> Test 900p, a 40 FPS cap, Medium textures, or Turbo mode separately, repeating the complete route after each change.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Choose the next adjustment from the weakest scene</h2>
    <div class="grid cols3">
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Stable baseline</span><h3>Keep 720p / 30 FPS</h3><p>Save the complete profile. Raise textures or one world-detail control before increasing several settings together.</p></section>
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Clarity test</span><h3>Try 900p</h3><p>Change only resolution and repeat the same base, traversal, fight, and multiplayer state. Return to 720p if the weakest segment becomes uneven.</p></section>
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Frame-rate test</span><h3>Try 40 FPS</h3><p>Change only the cap after the 30 FPS route passes. Keep it only when the busiest base and combat segment remain acceptable.</p></section>
    </div>

    <h2>Fix common Palworld problems on ROG Ally</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Check first</th><th>Next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Populated base misses the cap</td><td>Restore 720p, Low, Performance mode, and the same active-Pal count</td><td>Reduce world detail and effects; compare the same base before changing the cap or power mode</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Traversal hitches</td><td>Confirm SSD storage, adequate free space, no background downloads, and the Low baseline</td><td>Restart and repeat the exact route before changing texture or view-distance settings</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Multi-Pal combat becomes uneven</td><td>Restore Low effects, shadows, grass, and a single frame limiter</td><td>Keep 30 FPS and retest without capture overlays or background work</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Multiplayer feels delayed</td><td>Compare input and world response in the same area offline as a diagnostic</td><td>Check server and network conditions separately; do not assume every delay is GPU load</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Image is too soft</td><td>Confirm only one scaling path is active</td><td>Try a clearer in-game quality mode at 720p, then compare 900p separately</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Controller prompts or inputs are wrong</td><td>Set Armoury Crate control mode to Gamepad or Auto</td><td>Restore default Steam Input and game controls, then disconnect extra controllers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Turbo is unavailable through a dock</td><td>Connect the original or a compatible charger directly</td><td>Isolate dock and cable; verify USB-C PD output, passthrough, port sharing, and cable rating</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Performance changed after an update</td><td>Restart and restore the photographed baseline</td><td>Verify files and record the current game, driver, BIOS, and Armoury Crate versions</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Ally versus Ally X memory, battery, and storage planning</h2>
    <p>ASUS lists a 40Wh battery and 16GB memory for the original 2023 Ally, while its 2024 Ally X page lists an 80Wh battery and 24GB memory. Both official pages list a 1080p/120Hz display and a 65W adapter. Those differences do not prove a universal Palworld frame rate or a fixed runtime ratio: game world, active Pals, multiplayer state, operating mode, software, memory allocation, brightness, battery condition, and thermals still matter.</p>
    <p>Steam currently lists <strong>40GB of available space</strong>, an SSD requirement, 16GB minimum system memory, broadband internet, multiplayer, online co-op, cross-platform multiplayer, Steam Cloud, Workshop support, and full controller support. Leave room beyond 40GB for updates, worlds, shader data, Workshop content, captures, and Windows temporary files. Check the live install estimate and plan the library with the <a href="/calculators/storage-planner/">storage planner</a> and <a href="/guides/rog-ally-ssd-size-compatibility-upgrade/">ROG Ally SSD compatibility guide</a>.</p>
    <p>This page does not invent battery hours. Measure the complete route at matched conditions, then use the <a href="/calculators/battery-estimator/">battery estimator</a> or <a href="/guides/rog-ally-battery-life-calculator-guide/">ROG Ally calculator guide</a>. Stabilize handheld play before using the <a href="/guides/rog-ally-dock-tv-monitor-setup/">ROG Ally dock and TV guide</a>.</p>

    <h2>Optional gear after the profile is stable</h2>
    <p class="affiliate-note">Disclosure: these are broad Amazon searches marked sponsored/nofollow, not hands-on endorsements. Compare exact specifications, model fit, seller traceability, warranty, and return terms. No price, compatibility, performance, or battery claim is made; a real Associates tag is appended only when configured.</p>
    <div class="grid cols3">
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=rog+ally+x+external+ssd+usb+c+10gbps" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="nvme-ssds"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>USB-C external SSD storage</h3><p class="muted">Compare sustained transfer behavior, enclosure heat, cable rating, capacity, warranty, and exact-device support.</p></a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=rog+ally+x+65w+usb+c+pd+charger" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="chargers"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>65W-class Ally chargers</h3><p class="muted">Verify dedicated-port USB-C PD output, included cable rating, port-sharing behavior, seller traceability, and warranty.</p></a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=rog+ally+usb+c+pd+dock+ethernet" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="docks"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>ROG Ally docks with Ethernet</h3><p class="muted">Check PD passthrough, host-cable reach, physical clearance, Ethernet support, ventilation, and display modes.</p></a>
    </div>
    <p>Compare categories in the <a href="/gear/">spec-based gear library</a>, follow the <a href="/guides/rog-ally-x-accessories-buying-checklist/">ROG Ally X accessory checklist</a>, or set a limit with the <a href="/calculators/accessory-budget/">accessory budget calculator</a>.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="grid cols2">
      {faqs.map(faq => <section class="card"><h3>{faq.question}</h3><p>{faq.answer}</p></section>)}
    </div>

    <h2>Sources and methodology</h2>
    <p>Sources were fetched successfully on August 23, 2026. Steam’s current public product data supplied the July 9, 2026 release date, Pocketpair developer/publisher identity, 40GB storage and SSD requirements, 16GB minimum memory, note that performance may vary with active Pals, multiplayer/Workshop/Steam Cloud labels, full-controller-support label, and official image. Pocketpair supplies the official game site. ASUS supplied its Operating Mode guidance and official original Ally and Ally X battery, memory, display, and adapter specifications.</p>
    <p>The settings are a conservative editorial test sequence derived from those public constraints and normal graphics-diagnosis practice. Handheld Settings Lab did not personally benchmark the current game, world, server, Ally model, Windows build, driver, BIOS, Armoury Crate version, memory allocation, battery, or thermals. The 30 and 40 FPS figures are targets to test, not measured guarantees; no fixed-runtime or search-volume claim is made.</p>
    <ul>{sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">{source.label}</a></li>)}</ul>
    <p>Return to the <a href="/rog-ally-settings/">ROG Ally settings hub</a>, compare the general <a href="/steam-deck-settings/palworld/">Steam Deck</a> and dedicated <a href="/legion-go-settings/palworld/">Legion Go</a> pages, use the <a href="/calculators/">battery, storage, and accessory calculators</a>, or browse the <a href="/gear/">gear library</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
